{number: 56}
{title: Bringing In The Sheaves}
{key: C}

{start_of_verse: 1}
[C] Sowing in the morning, sowing seeds of kindness,
Sowing in the noontide and the dewy [G7] eve;
[C] Waiting for the harvest, and the time of reaping,
We shall come re-[G7] joicing, bringing in the [C] sheaves.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
Bringing in the [F] sheaves, bringing in the [C] sheaves,
We shall come re-[G7] joicing, bringing in the [C] sheaves;
Bringing in the [F] sheaves, bringing in the [C] sheaves,
We shall come re-[G7] joicing, bringing in the [C] sheaves.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: 2}
[C] Sowing in the sunshine, sowing in the shadows,
Fearing neither clouds nor winter's chilling [G7] breeze;
[C] By and by the harvest, and the labor ended,
We shall come re-[G7] joicing, bringing in the [C] sheaves.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
[C] Going forth with weeping, sowing for the Master,
Tho' the loss sustained our spirit often [G7] grieves;
[C] When our weeping's over, He will bid us welcome,
We shall come re-[G7] joicing, bringing in the [C] sheaves.
{end_of_verse}
